IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ea-cpc-interface`
IMPORT `ea-types`

-- Evidence Act 1893, Part 2, sections 93 to 102: exclusion of oral by documentary evidence.
-- Source: source/EA1893.txt lines 2871 to 3103.
--
-- The question this module answers: WHEN IS ORAL OR OTHER EVIDENCE EXCLUDED BECAUSE THE TERMS OF A
-- CONTRACT, GRANT, OTHER DISPOSITION OF PROPERTY, OR MATTER REQUIRED BY LAW TO BE IN A DOCUMENT, ARE
-- IN THE DOCUMENT?  These sections are mostly civil in their working, but they apply in any proceeding
-- to which Parts 1, 2 and 3 apply (section 2(1)), including a prosecution that turns on a document.

§ `93. Terms reduced to a document`

-- 93: where the terms of a contract, grant or other disposition of property have been reduced by or by
-- consent of the parties to the form of a document, and in all cases in which a matter is required by law
-- to be reduced to the form of a document, no evidence may be given in proof of the terms or matter except
-- the document itself, or secondary evidence of its contents where that is admissible under the Act.
-- Exception 1: a public officer required by law to be appointed in writing, where it is shown that a person
-- has acted as such, need not have the writing proved.  Exception 2: wills admitted to probate in Singapore
-- may be proved by the probate.  Explanation 3: the statement in a document of a fact other than the facts
-- referred to in the section does not preclude oral evidence of the same fact.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 93, Exceptions 1 and 2, Explanation 3"
GIVEN p IS A `Parol Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 93 confines proof to the document` IF
        (   p's `the terms of a contract, grant or other disposition of property have been reduced by or by consent of the parties to the form of a document`
         OR p's `the matter is required by law to be reduced to the form of a document`)
    AND NOT p's `a public officer is required by law to be appointed in writing and it is shown that a particular person has acted as such officer`
    AND NOT p's `the will has been admitted to probate in Singapore`
    AND NOT p's `the fact to be proved is a fact other than the terms of the contract, grant or disposition, or the matter, required to be in a document`

§ `94. Exclusion of evidence of oral agreement`

-- 94: when the terms have been proved according to section 93, no evidence of any oral agreement or statement
-- is to be admitted as between the parties to the instrument or their representatives in interest for the
-- purpose of contradicting, varying, adding to or subtracting from its terms, subject to six provisos:
-- (a) any fact that would invalidate the document or entitle a person to a decree or order relating to it;
-- (b) a separate oral agreement as to a matter on which the document is silent and which is not inconsistent
-- with its terms (the court having regard to the formality of the document); (c) a separate oral agreement
-- constituting a condition precedent to the attaching of an obligation; (d) a distinct subsequent oral
-- agreement to rescind or modify, except where the contract is by law required to be in writing or has been
-- registered; (e) a usage or custom annexing incidents not expressly mentioned, except where repugnant to or
-- inconsistent with the express terms; (f) any fact showing how the language of the document is related to
-- existing facts.  Proviso (b)'s regard to the degree of formality is a matter for the court and is not a
-- fact here.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 94 and provisos (a) to (f)"
GIVEN p IS A `Parol Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 94 excludes the oral agreement or statement` IF
        p's `the terms of the document have been proved according to section 93`
    AND p's `the evidence is of an oral agreement or statement`
    AND p's `the evidence is offered as between the parties to the instrument or their representatives in interest`
    AND p's `the evidence is for the purpose of contradicting, varying, adding to or subtracting from the terms of the document`
    AND NOT p's `the fact would invalidate the document or entitle a person to a decree or order relating to it`
    AND NOT p's `the evidence is of a separate oral agreement as to a matter on which the document is silent and which is not inconsistent with its terms`
    AND NOT p's `the evidence is of a separate oral agreement constituting a condition precedent to the attaching of an obligation under the document`
    AND NOT (   p's `the evidence is of a distinct subsequent oral agreement to rescind or modify the contract, grant or disposition`
            AND NOT p's `the contract, grant or disposition is by law required to be in writing, or has been registered according to the law in force as to the registration of documents`)
    AND NOT (   p's `the evidence is of a usage or custom by which incidents not expressly mentioned in a contract are usually annexed to contracts of that description`
            AND NOT p's `annexing the incident would be repugnant to or inconsistent with the express terms of the contract`)
    AND NOT p's `the evidence is of a fact which shows in what manner the language of the document is related to existing facts`

§ `95 to 100. Evidence to explain or amend a document`

-- 95: when the language is on its face ambiguous or defective, evidence may not be given of facts which would
-- show its meaning or supply its defects.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 95"
GIVEN p IS A `Parol Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 95 excludes evidence of facts showing the meaning or supplying the defects` IF
    p's `the language used in the document is on its face ambiguous or defective`

-- 96: when the language is plain in itself and applies accurately to existing facts, evidence may not be given
-- to show that it was not meant to apply to those facts.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 96"
GIVEN p IS A `Parol Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 96 excludes evidence that the language was not meant to apply to the existing facts` IF
    p's `the language used in the document is plain in itself and applies accurately to existing facts`

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 97"
GIVEN p IS A `Parol Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 97 permits evidence that the language was used in a peculiar sense` IF
    p's `the language used in the document is plain in itself but meaningless in reference to existing facts`

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 98"
GIVEN p IS A `Parol Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 98 permits evidence of facts showing to which person or thing the language applies` IF
    p's `the language might have been meant to apply to any one, and could not have been meant to apply to more than one, of several persons or things`

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 99"
GIVEN p IS A `Parol Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 99 permits evidence of which of 2 sets of facts the language was meant to apply to` IF
    p's `the language applies partly to one set of existing facts and partly to another, and the whole of it does not apply correctly to either`

@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 100"
GIVEN p IS A `Parol Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 100 permits evidence of the meaning of the characters or expressions` IF
    p's `the evidence is to show the meaning of illegible or not commonly intelligible characters, or of foreign, obsolete, technical, local or provincial expressions, abbreviations or words used in a peculiar sense`

§ `101 and 102. Third persons; wills`

-- 101: persons who are not parties to a document, or their representatives in interest, may give evidence of
-- any fact tending to show a contemporaneous agreement varying the terms of the document.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 101"
GIVEN p IS A `Parol Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 101 permits the third person's evidence of a contemporaneous agreement` IF
        p's `the evidence is given by a person who is not a party to the document or a representative in interest of a party`
    AND p's `the evidence is of a fact tending to show a contemporaneous agreement varying the terms of the document`

-- 102: nothing in sections 93 to 101 affects the construction of wills.
@ref "Evidence Act 1893, s 102"
GIVEN p IS A `Parol Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sections 93 to 101 do not apply because the question is the construction of a will` IF
    p's `the question is as to the construction of a will`
